<!--Post: 9898--><!--Time: 1109697009-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9898"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 9:10 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tom will do his own thing, and frankly, there&#39;s still a huge load of things to discuss and learn about DTDC® <i>&#40;Denny The Dog Catcher®&#41;</i>, but are there suggestions for other mystery killers to investigate once the former BTK has been sealed away?  <BR> <BR>I&#39;ll pony up my own; the East Area Rapist/Original Night Stalker. He was just as vicious as BTK, and maybe more prolific. The current site about EAR/ONS is okay, but Tom does, to my eye, bring a strong aesthetic in site design and an ability to get the info out there that other webmasters who pursue similar subjects don&#39;t possess. Only a suggestion, submitted respectfully. <BR> <BR>Any others?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9898-->
<!--Post: 9911--><!--Time: 1109701822-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9911"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 10:30 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I am very intrested in a string of murders that happened in Lewiston, Idaho. They happened in the seventies and eighties. EARS/ONS is intresting however I believe he is dead. Of course alot of people thought the same of BTK, so? I think Tom will resume his Zodiac search which is still unfinished.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9911-->
<!--Post: 9934--><!--Time: 1109707704-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9934"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 12:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Considering two of my locals: <BR> <BR>Vermont-  Bennington Triangle case.  Several disapperances in such a short time makes people wonder what happened to these people.  Only one body was ever found. <BR> <BR>Ohio- Torso Murder case-  Tens of body parts found, and only two victims identified.  This case has never been solved. <BR> <BR>The two cases though are very loose and not well formed at all.  I&#39;m actually trying to get information on the Bennington Triangle case.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9934-->
<!--Post: 9936--><!--Time: 1109707810-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9936"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 12:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->When I was a young boy growing up in Modesto, the EAR was our local boogey man. He struck in my neighborhood... just a couple blocks down from our house.  To this day I remember my mom and her friends talking about EAR in hurried voices and hushed tones. <BR> <BR>I visit the current EAR site &#40;mostly to surf the msg board&#41; once in a while, but would love to really turn over some rocks on this guy.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9936-->
<!--Post: 9945--><!--Time: 1109711916-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9945"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tbear<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tbear<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 1:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The I-45 corridor murders is what I would enjoy getting into. A lot of kidnapped and murdered females. Many unsolved cases and no central agency working on them. So nobody has been able to piece together exactly how many are actually tied together and it&#39;s been going on for years from Galveston past Dallas.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9945-->
<!--Post: 10025--><!--Time: 1109730096-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10025"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 6:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Steve and Armchair, <BR> <BR>I can just about see the roof of the Harrington house in the distance. <BR>The little speck of terra cotta in a breathtaking swath of creation was a veil for one of the most brutal homicides that ever rocked the O.C.   <BR> <BR>Niguel Shores is a guard-gated coastal enclave in the Monarch Beach area of Dana Point. <BR> <BR>It&#39;s a logistical nightmare for a burglar. High walls, bright street lights, vigilant neighbors, security. EAR/ONS choice defies all reason and, if it’s possible, makes the Harrington murders all the more terrifying. <BR> <BR>Scheb, I hope to God he’s dead. <BR> <BR>Serial killers are a virus. The Pacific Northwest, The Ukraine and of course, the Midwest. <BR> <BR>TV’s next target? <BR> <BR>Man, I hate to say this, hate it – BTK has probably whelped a pup, an unvaccinated rabid mongrel with a gruesome lineage. If this one needs attention the way his sire did, then he knows how to get it. <BR> <BR>The fact that Denny was a communicator and could not resist the limelight, made him vulnerable in the information age. <BR> <BR>In a pop culture that beatifies one-upsmanship, another menace can’t be far behind. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10025-->
<!--Post: 10046--><!--Time: 1109735763-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10046"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 7:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I like the I-45 idea too. I lived in Dickinson when some of the skeletal remains were found and when some of the girls went missing. I know a Galv. S.O. officer. Perhaps I can get some info from him. He knows that I am ruthless when it comes to pursuit. <BR> <BR>Or, we can comb the waters for Morris Black&#39;s head. I&#39;ll bet that it has a bullet hole in the back of the skull. Robert Durst would know.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10046-->
<!--Post: 10057--><!--Time: 1109737284-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10057"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 8:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><i>&#34;...Serial killers are a virus. The Pacific Northwest, The Ukraine and of course, the Midwest. <BR> <BR>TV’s next target? <BR> <BR>Man, I hate to say this, hate it – BTK has probably whelped a pup, an unvaccinated rabid mongrel with a gruesome lineage. If this one needs attention the way his sire did, then he knows how to get it. <BR> <BR>The fact that Denny was a communicator and could not resist the limelight, made him vulnerable in the information age. <BR> <BR>In a pop culture that beatifies one-upsmanship, another menace can’t be far behind...&#34;</i> <BR> <BR>Well said, Lost one. <BR> <BR>I&#39;ve gotta say that I&#39;m glad a couple of y&#39;all mentioned the I-45 murders. It appears Police in the area are befuddled by the whole thing; is it just a murder magnet, is it one highly productive psycho, is it more than one?  <BR> <BR>It&#39;s a damn good case to examine, I agree. EAR/ONS is interesting because of his viciousness, his sheer invisibility. Think about it...no one connected his crimes until several years after the fact. And then there is, at that site, the tape of him. A real nightmare to hit play on your machine and hear that hissing evil come through.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10057-->
<!--Post: 10146--><!--Time: 1109785349-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10146"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tbear<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tbear<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 9:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok, you got me, Steve.  Possibly Tom wants to look at another Cold Case in his back yard? BTK got 30 years, EAR/ONS&#39;s time running out? Bring it on. I think a little web attention Tom Voight style may help this case out. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10146-->
<!--Post: 10151--><!--Time: 1109786551-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10151"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:linnieskid@earthlink.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Linnieskid<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Linnieskid<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 10:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Go Tbear Go!  EAR/ONS should be next on the list. <BR>Armchair:  I would not only like to turn over some rocks on this guy but throw some rocks as well.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10151-->
<!--Post: 10156--><!--Time: 1109786958-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10156"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:linnieskid@earthlink.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Linnieskid<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Linnieskid<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 10:09 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Steve: We can only hope that Tom will dig into the EAR/ONS story with the same fire as he did with BTK. &#40; If I were him, I&#39;d be dragging my a$$&#41; LOL.. Forums of this sort will  bring the story to the forefront. As an intended victim <BR> &#40;I believe&#41; I want to see him brought down!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10156-->
<!--Post: 10165--><!--Time: 1109791974-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10165"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 11:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><i>&#34;...I think a little web attention Tom Voight style may help this case out...&#34;</i> <BR> <BR>I agree, but I want to emphasize I&#39;m not pushing for Tom to do any one thing - I know full well from my own experience blogging that it&#39;s about following your <i>own</i> lights in the end. I blogged about BTK, for instance, because I just couldn&#39;t help but be fascinated with the amount of evidence available, knowing that it was still a great mystery. I wanted to know what kind of mind a BTK might have, too. <BR> <BR>The cases that catch me still are Zodiac - just like Tom that way - EAR/ONS, and the I-45 murders. But I wanted to say my suggestion was only that, a suggestion. There is already a site about EAR/ONS, and it&#39;s decent. It just doesn&#39;t have Tom&#39;s touch for catching your interest the moment you click to the homepage - I don&#39;t know about you all, but the first time I came to catchbtk that stark screen with the shadowy figure and the low music got my interest immediately.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10165-->
<!--Post: 10172--><!--Time: 1109793509-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10172"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lakesguy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lakesguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 11:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->How about the Oakland County &#40;MI&#41; Child slayings from the mid-70&#39;s? The killer was nicknamed &#39;The Babysitter.&#39; The police have started re-examining old evidence, etc. This is a case that needs the sane, compelling, extremely competent Tom Voigt style. What&#39;s out there now, on this particular case, is anything but sane, compelling or competent. <BR> <BR>I also would love to see Tom create a site about the EAR/ONS as well. There&#39;s a true monster for you...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10172-->
<!--Post: 10197--><!--Time: 1109808601-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10197"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 4:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lostdog:  The fact that the next Dennis Radish wannabe could be out there somewhere is a chilling thought that hadn&#39;t occurred to me. No doubt, you&#39;re right, though.  The Web is just another medium.  Jack the Ripper scrawled on a wall &#40;well, maybe it was him&#41;.  Today&#39;s sociopaths have the Web. <BR> <BR>There&#39;s probably a certain subgroup that would be most likely to take to the Web like a duck to water though &#40;nope, not a reference to any of Rader&#39;s brothers&#41;:  the ones with a pronounced streak of narcissism.  The same type who have always played up to the traditional media, like Manson, or who try to publish their accounts of the crimes for money &#40;Berkowitz, Unterweger, I think Canadian SK Clifford Olsen tried it too&#41;. <BR> <BR>Rader really went out of his way to court the attention.  He practically demanded a manhunt.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10197-->
<!--Post: 10284--><!--Time: 1109873629-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10284"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 10:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.geocities.com/verbal_plainfield/coldcases/coldcases.html" target=_top>http://www.geocities.com/verbal_plainfield/coldcas es/coldcases.html</a> <BR> <BR>I suggest the Alphabet Murders ... That one has a weird angle.  First name, Last name, and Town that they wre found in all began with the same letter. <BR> <BR>I DON&#39;T suggest the New Orleans Axe murderers.  Though the way they described it seems clean cut, that case is actually horribly disorganized.  The society there at the time had a thing for blaming someone else.  Now this isn&#39;t &#34;send in a tip to the WPD on ideas you have to find BTK&#34; blaming ... this was more like &#34;I know he did it!  I have a grudge on him!  He did it!&#34; The case is really confusing in that regard .... <BR> <BR>As for the Lover&#39;s Lane murders and Texarkana murders:  A very much &#34;Zodiac&#34; feel to it.  Just without the letters from a huge ego. <BR> <BR>Oklahoma&#39;s State Fair Murders is another one that happened recent enough that a killer may be brought to justice.  &#40;Unlike the Axeman murders where if the killer was still alive he&#39;s drinking water from an IV unit in an old folk&#39;s home&#41; <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10284-->
<!--Post: 10296--><!--Time: 1109880160-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10296"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tbear<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tbear<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 12:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->not finding any info, just the agatha christie alphabet murders. link isn&#39;t working. I admit I am curious.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10296-->
<!--Post: 10360--><!--Time: 1109913115-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10360"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 9:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The Lewiston Valley serial case in Idaho has recently been reopened. For those not familar with it, in Sept. of 1982 3 people vanished on the same night near the Lewiston Civic Theater. The two females bodies where found but the third body of a missing male have never been recovered. <BR>The police where able to connect these murders with the disappearence of a 12 year old girl from Asotin, Washington. She went missing from the Astonin County Fair in 1979. A 22 year old college student from Lewiston was murdered in 1981. Her dismembered body was found along the banks of the Snake River in Clarkston. The police have a long standing prime suspect but have never made an arrest. This suspect was questioned several years ago by F.B.I. about the Spokane Washington serial case unsolved at that time. He was of course cleared of all wrong doing in that case.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10360-->
<!--Post: 10570--><!--Time: 1110012194-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10570"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 05, 2005 - 12:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks, SC, for telling about the Lewiston Valley case...I agree, it is interesting, and creepy. <BR> <BR>This doesn&#39;t come under the heading of being a suggestion - the crimes and criminals are European - but it does fall under the headings &#34;interesting&#34; and &#34;unsolved&#34;. <BR> <BR>Here&#39;s a link to a blog entry I wrote about the guy; <a href="http://www.planethuff.com/darkside/archives/true_crime_unsolved/index.html#a000593">&#34;TBK...The River Hate...&#34;</a> <BR> <BR>See, Mons, Belgium, has a yet-to-be caught serial of it&#39;s own. In method of operation he&#39;s got more in common with the Cleveland Torso Killer, but when it comes to elusiveness, attention to detail, communication with the press, and some other things, this guy seems almost like a European kissin&#39; cousin to our dear old Denny the Dog Catcher.  <BR> <BR>To top it off, the Belgians took to calling this serial the &#34;Trash Bag Killer&#34;. In french that reads &#34;Tueur De Sac De Détritus&#34;, which is pretty uninteresting. But in english, as you can see, we come back to that danged ole T, B, K.  <BR> <BR>We Americans have a knack for snappy acronyms, y&#39; know? Even our serial killers have brand-name recognition.  <BR> <BR>Anyway - read the blog entry, or do a google on &#34;Trash Bag Killer&#34;, or maybe even &#34;Butcher of Mons&#34;. Like BTK, TBK also went quiet for a bit. You ask me, if he&#39;s still around he&#39;s just bought a nice big freezer, and all his catches are bagged up, neatly hacksawed apart, in that freezer.  <BR> <BR>Those crazy Europeans. Next time you hear or read someone snarking about us decadent Americans and our epidemics of serial murder, just remember Belgium&#39;s very own TBK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10570-->
<!--Post: 10574--><!--Time: 1110029314-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10574"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 05, 2005 - 5:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Trash bags seem to be a popular form of disposal, I remember a case in the early eighties with the same MO but left the remains along highway rest stops near New York and New Jersey. This case was also unsolved. These where male victims however, homosexual murders victims,  I think. The names of the drop sites would seem to have some meaning to the killer. I would suggest someone with satanic leanings or hate groups<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10574-->
<!--Post: 10580--><!--Time: 1110031634-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10580"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sidewalker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sidewalker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 05, 2005 - 6:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->ear/ons <BR>one freaky sick human. <BR>That case really scares the u-no outta me.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10580-->
<!--Post: 10634--><!--Time: 1110072848-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10634"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 05, 2005 - 5:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The East Area Rapist/ Original Night Stalker seems viable. The perpetrator would most probably be in his mid to late 40s. He made the transition from a serial rapist to a serial murderer and the locale was California, the global capital of serial murder. All the ingredients for another adventure.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10634-->
<!--Post: 10693--><!--Time: 1110142473-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10693"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 06, 2005 - 12:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->lol Oh my God I am still stuck in the Kansas cold case files and missing persons, trying to figure out how many nuts came back after the war and were still killing, Rader didn&#39;t have time to kill all 48 of these people, Anyway, I will help were ever I can, there are approx. 20 serial killers in the us right now, In the Serial Killer #2 thread I added a link to national news on this subject, I just hope they others are not into puzzles lol. Sorry can&#39;t help. I can&#39;t stay up all night anymore trying to solve puzzles, my family has been verrrrrryyyyy patient  E.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10693-->
<!--Post: 11830--><!--Time: 1111241778-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11830"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dlee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dlee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 19, 2005 - 6:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I live about 30 miles from Lewiston,and was just at the Lewiston Civic Theater&#40;it figures prominently in in a triple abduction/murder central to the case&#41; for a program my daughter was involved in.I hadnt been in there for 20 years since I was in a production there in &#39;86.I remember the murders were still a hot topic of conversation among the cast and crew then. <BR>Very creepy wandering around in that Gothic Old barn knowing what probably happened there...Hasnt changed a bit. <BR>Facinating case. A few months ago a team of &#39;psychic detectives&#39; were in town trying to locate the remains of the 12 year old girl who disapeared during the Asotin Fair in 1979. <BR>They poked around in the brush by the Snake River for awhile and left town empty handed according to the paper. <BR>Yeah I think anyone interested in Zodiac or BTK would find this case of interest.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11830-->
<!--Post: 11841--><!--Time: 1111261035-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11841"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bbyrum9@foothill.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 19, 2005 - 11:37 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The I 45 cases, Lewiston, and EAR seem to be the most logical, for the Western half of the country. What if someone could tie the Cabin 28 job in with Lewiston?? That would make it very palatable in the eyes of the general public. <BR>EAR is the most mysterious. We don&#39;t know when he started or where, or with what type of offense. We are now getting questions as to wheather or not he is even the same person. He would be around 52 1/2 years old right now, give or take 3 years. He could be dead, that&#39;s about 50-50 right now. Or he could have just stopped, and just like Denny, is living right among us. Maybe even right here in Sacramento. I&#39;d say given the totality of what we think we know about him, and what we know we DON&#39;T know about him, he is the most prolific UNP serial offender West of the Misissippi in maybe the last 40 years.   <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11841-->
<!--Post: 11849--><!--Time: 1111279460-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11849"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 19, 2005 - 4:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->go read plane crash thread, I have been looking for The name lewis thank you all<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11849-->
<!--Post: 11874--><!--Time: 1111324783-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11874"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 20, 2005 - 5:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dlee, <BR>I am intrested in the long time suspect police have in this case. Do you have any information on him. You are the first person I have spoken to who lives near Lewiston. Any additional info you have on the case, I would appreciate you posting.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11874-->
<!--Post: 11895--><!--Time: 1111365677-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11895"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 20, 2005 - 4:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dlee, I need to tye this case into soemthing else going on here on the board, can you give us more information on it Thanks E.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11895-->
<!--Post: 11898--><!--Time: 1111368884-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11898"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 20, 2005 - 5:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Re: Lewiston <BR> <BR>I am assuming that there is a reason that the male, who was never found, was eliminated as the prime suspect. Can someone fill that in for me?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11898-->
<!--Post: 11916--><!--Time: 1111403147-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11916"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dlee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dlee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 21, 2005 - 3:05 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Scbenson, <BR>Yeah, I live just up the river in Orofino where I work as a State Correctional officer. <BR>I lived in the same Normal Hill neighborhood just up the street from the Civic Theater in 85-86 and was involved in a production there in the Spring of &#39;86. <BR>As far as the suspect goes im afraid you probably know as much about him as I do.I know the police linked him to the Asotin Fair disapearence in &#39;79 and the Theater as an employee in &#39;82. <BR>I understand he was a long time valley resident and that he recently moved - where I dont know.All of which begs the question why no indictment? <BR>I dont know if a case of suspect tunnel vision may have set in during the investigation.I hope not.I dont know his name. <BR>One of my fellow cast members claimed to be a suspect at one point whether that was true I dont know. <BR>The young man who disapeared&#40;I believe his name was Pearsol?&#41;was eliminated as a suspect because he had no vehicle,just a twelve speed bike. <BR>Among other reasons. <BR>He also worked at the theater and had told friends that he was going to the theater to do some laundry the same night the two young women disappeared. <BR>His clothes were found in the dryer he was never seen again. <BR>Then of course nearly two years later the two women&#39;s remains were discovered twenty miles away over an embankment up the Julieta canyon.&#40;hard to transport two bodies up there on a bike.&#41; <BR>Embersage,Im really not an authority by any means on the case but if youll tell me what info your looking for Ill try to help, you or Scbenson can email me at <a href="mailto:dlee@corr.state.id.us">dlee@corr.state.id.us</a> <BR>Scbenson are you familair with the layout of the Theater and its surroundings?If so I have a pet theory as to where the killer intercepted and either lured or forced the two girls into the building. Ill share if your interested. <BR>Its just speculation though.  <BR>Speaking of Lewiston Valley cold cases are you familiar with the Lonnie Jones Abduction /Murder from 1951? Thats another weird one.This one connected to the Clearwater County Fair. This time a 12 year old boy.Im certain however there is no connection between the two cases.   <BR> <BR>     <BR>  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11916-->
<!--Post: 11989--><!--Time: 1111488714-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11989"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 22, 2005 - 2:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m not familar with the area at all. Have never even seen photos. Would love to hear your theory. Do you think they where actually killed in the theatre? Never heard of the Lonnie Jones case sounds like fair in that area of the country can be dangerous. I did not know Pearsol worked at the theatre. Very intresting. I knew he was known to have last been seen in that area. Keep me posted if you remember anything else. I have always been interested in this case.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11989-->
<!--Post: 11998--><!--Time: 1111498794-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11998"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dlee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dlee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 22, 2005 - 5:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Im Going to start a thread to answer this since this one is getting long.&#40;If Tom doesnt mind.&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11998-->
